WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.180
Strap in, Marvel fans there's more Thor in
store.

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:06.340
Per The Hollywood Reporter, a fourth Thor
film is in the works.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.340
The good news?

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.660
Thor: Ragnarok filmmaker Taika Waititi is
officially on board to write and direct Thor

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:16.110
4, meaning that he can continue imbuing the
film series with his signature humor, eccentric

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:17.340
wit, and snappy dialogue.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.080
"This doesn't make any sense.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.580
No, nothing makes sense here, man.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.200
The only thing that does make sense is that
nothing makes sense."

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:25.060
The bad news?

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:29.210
Waititi singing on for another Thor film means
that the live-action adaptation of Akira is

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.690
now on hold but if you’ve been following
the development of that movie at all, what

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:33.690
else is new, right?

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:38.630
A feature film translation of Katsuhiro Otomo's
manga of the same name, Akira has been in

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:44.220
development for years, experiencing an upswing
in May 2019 when Waititi boarded as its director

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.400
and co-writer.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:49.690
After since 2002 to get the movie off the
ground, studio Warner Bros. finally scheduled

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:52.920
it to debut in theaters on May 21, 2021.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:57.280
Prior to joining Thor 4, Waititi was said
to be testing actors in a talent search that

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.390
spanned the globe, and things seemed to be
finally moving forward for Akira.

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:05.700
Unfortunately, the film is on an indefinite
hold now that Waititi is focusing on Thor

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:09.860
4, which will reportedly rub shoulders with
Akira's planned production start date.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:13.460
With the two start dates for filming now being
so close to each other, it seems there's no

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:16.540
way Waititi could feasibly work on both projects.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:21.380
It's unclear what will happen to Akira while
Waititi is writing and directing Thor 4, but

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:26.120
THR has reported that Warner Bros. intends
to keep Waititi attached to the project, apparently

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:27.420
on a long-term basis.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:32.170
Executives are reportedly hoping that Waititi
will re-commit to Akira after he wraps the

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:32.820
new Thor movie.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.380
Fortunately for everyone, Chris Hemsworth
is lined up to reprise his role as the Asgardian

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:40.640
god of thunder who underwent a drastic transformation
in Avengers: Endgame.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:44.980
Thor's evolution from a cocky, arrogant hero
with little regard for those around him to

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:49.080
a kind-hearted, empathetic, funny guy who
overcomes personal struggles has impressed

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:52.870
viewers but the new physique he sported in
Endgame left fans divided.

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:55.140
Some loved "fat Thor," while others hated
him.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.710
He never did shed any weight in Endgame, last
appearing in the film with his beer belly

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:02.700
and shaggy hair firmly intact, and Hemsworth
couldn't be happier about that.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.700
He told Variety:

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.880
"I feel like we’ve opened up such a different
character.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.600
I feel more energized for the possibility
of where it could go."

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:13.409
Endgame came to a close with Thor appointing
Valkyrie as the protector of New Asgard, then

00:02:13.409 --> 00:02:16.680
joining the Guardians of the Galaxy on their
mission to locate Gamora.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:20.439
It's believed that Guardians of the Galaxy
Vol. 3, which has director James Gunn back

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:24.640
on board, will focus on the Guardians as they
track down their green-skinned teammate, with

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.560
Thor possibly in the mix as well as an ally,
or even new member of the team.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.599
What happens in that film could influence
the story of Thor 4.

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:36.409
But with Marvel Studios’ fourth phase of
the MCU being so shrouded in mystery, we truly

00:02:36.409 --> 00:02:38.930
have zero idea what will happen in either
film.

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:42.870
What's interesting about Thor 4 is that it's
the first instance in which an original Avenger

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.859
is continuing their standalone franchise beyond
a trilogy.

00:02:45.859 --> 00:02:50.629
Iron Man actor Robert Downey Jr. and Captain
America star Chris Evans each had three solo

00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:54.640
films in addition to crossover ensembles,
and both retired their characters with Avengers:

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:55.160
Endgame.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:02:59.480
"I am Iron Man."

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:04.100
This development begs a rather juicy question:
did Chris Hemsworth extend his contract to

00:03:04.109 --> 00:03:05.230
more solo movies?

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:07.260
How many Marvel films did he commit to?

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:10.760
It's all very exciting to think about, as
Hemsworth's Thor has become one of the most

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:15.569
charismatic and naturally hilarious heroes
in the MCU, arguably only becoming a serious

00:03:15.569 --> 00:03:19.989
fan-favorite after his jokier characterization
in Waititi’s Thor: Ragnarok.

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:23.320
We wouldn't mind a couple more Thor-featuring
flicks, and we doubt any other fans would

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:23.860
either.

